Desligamento por bateria ausente com fallback forcado.

check_battery_exist() pede orderly_poweroff(true) quando o PMIC diz que nao ha
bateria (fora dos modos META/ATE). Com STATIC_USERMODEHELPER o helper do Android
(/system_ext/bin/aee_core_forwarder) nao existia, o exec falhava e o kernel desligava
na hora. Sem ele (revisao rB) o kernel roda /sbin/poweroff (systemctl) e nao forca
mais nada: se o systemd travar, o aparelho fica ligado. Passa a usar
hw_protection_shutdown() (backport-reboot-hw-protection-shutdown.patch), que desliga a
forca 30 s depois, o mesmo prazo do caminho termico
(CONFIG_THERMAL_EMERGENCY_POWEROFF_DELAY_MS).

--- a/drivers/power/supply/mediatek/charger/mtk_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mediatek/charger/mtk_charger.c
@@ -1679,6 +1679,13 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * thunder: without STATIC_USERMODEHELPER, orderly_poweroff(true) runs
+ * /sbin/poweroff and forces nothing once that starts. Force the power-off
+ * if the orderly one has not finished after this delay.
+ */
+#define BATTERY_MISSING_POWEROFF_DELAY_MS	30000
+
 static void check_battery_exist(struct charger_manager *info)
 {
 	struct device *dev = NULL;
@@ -1722,7 +1729,8 @@
 				boot_mode);
 		else {
 			chr_err("battery doesn't exist, shutdown\n");
-			orderly_poweroff(true);
+			hw_protection_shutdown("Battery missing",
+					       BATTERY_MISSING_POWEROFF_DELAY_MS);
 		}
 	}
 }
